{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5ef","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":338,"recorded_at":1780531400000671,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"3d40ca8e-f983-4b50-af48-a64b76836461"},"task_id":"3d40ca8e-f983-4b50-af48-a64b76836461","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"3d40ca8e-f983-4b50-af48-a64b76836461","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(861 line(s) above)\n862|### 4.A TerminalBackend authority and terminology\n863|\n864|TerminalBackend is a host-local presentation and delegated process-hosting\n865|module. AX alone owns Logical Session identity and lineage, Owner and AX\n866|Replica roles, leases and fencing, provider lifecycle/native identity/store,\n867|workspace materialization, Checkpoints/evidence, task-board integration, mesh\n868|replication, and takeover. A backend owns exactly one host-local\n869|<dfn>Terminal Instance</dfn>: delegated PTY/process hosting, presentation,\n870|attach/reconnect, backend-local IPC, and backend-specific process observation.\n871|\n872|An <dfn>AX Replica</dfn> is a host holding synchronized durable AX state. A\n873|<dfn>presentation replica</dfn> or <dfn>client mirror</dfn> is only a view/input\n874|client of one Terminal Instance. Presentation replication MUST NOT create an AX\n875|Replica, acquire or renew a lease, change Owner, authorize input, or publish an\n876|owner-authored event. Schemas, CLI, UI, and logs MUST NOT use these terms\n877|interchangeably.\n878|\n879|Every backend-created runtime ultimately executes exactly\n880|<code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>; a raw provider command is forbidden as a\n881|durable entry point. A backend MUST NOT interpret ownership, start or resume a\n882|provider without AX authorization, replace AX/provider/workspace/Checkpoint/\n883|task-board/mesh state, or turn attach into a lease mutation. A valid takeover\n884|or owner resume MAY bind the same Logical Session to a different conforming\n885|destination backend without clone or fork; AX emits a new immutable binding,\n886|event, and evidence and never mutates history.\n887|\n888|### 4.B Registry, identity, discovery, and trust\n889|\n890|<code>terminal_backend_id</code> is 1–128 ASCII bytes matching\n891|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:[.-][a-z0-9]+)*</code>. The <code>ax.</code> namespace is\n892|reserved. Canonical built-ins are <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n893|<code>ax.conpty</code>. Third parties use a stable vendor-owned namespace. No\n894|normative Superlogical ID is reserved.\n895|\n896|Terminal Backend Manifest 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no\n897|other member is permitted:\n898|\n899|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n900|| --- | --- |\n901|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-manifest</code> |\n902|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n903|| <code>manifest_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n904|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n905|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver |\n906|| <code>protocol_versions</code> | sorted unique semver[1..32], each in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n907|| <code>platforms</code> | sorted unique enum[1..4] from <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> |\n908|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | <code>builtin_go|local_program|trusted_executable|native_runtime</code> |\n909|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest for <code>local_program</code> or <code>trusted_executable</code>; null otherwise |\n910|| <code>static_capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] whose <code>origin</code> is <code>static</code> |\n911|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest |\n912|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code>; non-empty extensions require a later contract version |\n913|\n914|Terminal Backend Probe 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable observation; no\n915|other member is permitted:\n916|\n917|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n918|| --- | --- |\n919|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-probe</code> |\n920|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n921|| <code>probe_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n922|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n923|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to the admitted Manifest |\n924|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver selected from the Manifest's <code>protocol_versions</code> |\n925|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | enum equal to the Manifest member |\n926|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest|null exactly equal to the Manifest member |\n927|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code>, contained in the Manifest's <code>platforms</code> |\n928|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] |\n929|| <code>availability</code> | <code>available|conditional|unavailable|unknown</code> |\n930|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest of the domain-separated raw generation |\n931|| <code>capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] |\n932|| <code>evidence_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..256] referencing Capability Evidence 1.0.0 |\n933|| <code>probed_at</code> | timestamp |\n934|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n935|\n936|The generation digest uses SHA-256 over UTF-8\n937|<code>ax-terminal-backend-generation-v1\\0</code> followed by the backend's\n938|host-local raw generation bytes; it neither reveals nor reconstructs that\n939|generation. Manifest-to-Probe reconciliation is the following closed rule. The\n940|Probe <code>terminal_backend_id</code>, <code>implementation_version</code>,\n941|<code>implementation_kind</code>, and <code>executable_digest</code> MUST equal\n942|the Manifest members; its <code>protocol_version</code> MUST be exactly one member\n943|of <code>protocol_versions</code>, and its <code>platform</code> MUST be exactly\n944|one member of <code>platforms</code>. Array-to-scalar selection is membership,\n945|not aggregate equality.\n946|\n947|Let <code>M[c]</code> be the one Manifest static claim for capability\n948|<code>c</code>, when present, and <code>P[c]</code> the one Probe claim. The\n949|declared sorted-unique constraints make a duplicate key invalid before this\n950|reconciliation runs. The complete keyed relation is:\n951|\n952|1. Every <code>M[c]</code> MUST have exactly one <code>P[c]</code>; omission is a\n953|   manifest/probe mismatch.\n954|2. <code>P[c].origin=static</code> is permitted only when <code>M[c]</code>\n955|   exists, and <code>P[c]</code> MUST then equal <code>M[c]</code> member for\n956|   member. It is a static echo, not a new observation.\n957|3. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> with an existing <code>M[c]</code> is a\n958|   generation-bound override. It is permitted only when\n959|   <code>M[c].generation_variable=true</code>; its <code>value</code> MAY differ,\n960|   while <code>generation_variable</code>, <code>dependent_operations</code>, and\n961|   <code>evidence_requirements</code> MUST remain equal to <code>M[c]</code> and\n962|   the capability registry row.\n963|4. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> without <code>M[c]</code> is a probed\n964|   addition. It is permitted only for a capability in the closed registry, and\n965|   its three registry-derived members MUST equal that row. A Probe cannot add\n966|   a claim with <code>origin=static</code>.\n967|5. A true <code>P[c]</code> is admitted only when unexpired Capability Evidence\n968|   bound to this exact Manifest/Probe tuple satisfies every listed evidence\n969|   requirement. The required fact mapping is\n970|   <code>conformance_fixture-&gt;fixture_passed</code>,\n971|   <code>runtime_probe-&gt;runtime_probe_passed</code>,\n972|   <code>credential_sentinel-&gt;sentinel_passed</code>,\n973|   <code>provider_auth_smoke-&gt;provider_auth_passed</code>, and\n974|   <code>policy_authorization-&gt;policy_checked</code>. A false claim has no\n975|   matching Capability Evidence because Evidence <code>value</code> is the\n976|   literal <code>true</code>.\n977|6. <code>evidence_ids</code> MUST be exactly the sorted unique IDs of all\n978|   returned Capability Evidence objects used by true <code>P</code> claims.\n979|   Every referenced object MUST name exactly one present true claim; an ID for\n980|   an absent or false claim, an unreferenced returned object, conflicting\n981|   evidence, or duplicate/conflicting claims invalidates the whole Probe.\n982|\n983|A partial, malformed, stale, or failed Manifest, Probe, or evidence read is an\n984|error, never absence or availability. Any failed equality, membership, keyed\n985|relation, evidence binding, or evidence coverage rule is\n986|<code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code> and fails before\n987|activation; executable substitution or implementation drift additionally maps\n988|to its more specific Section 15.3 code.\n989|\n990|Discovery completes before activation. Duplicate/ambiguous IDs,\n991|manifest/probe disagreement, implementation drift, untrusted executable\n992|substitution, stale generation, unknown identity/version, or unevidenced claims\n993|fail closed. A manifest is not availability proof. External adapters use argv\n994|and local length-prefixed framing: unsigned 32-bit big-endian byte length plus\n995|UTF-8 JSON, at most 1 MiB, one request/response at a time. EOF, oversize,\n996|invalid JSON, unsolicited output, or deadline expiry terminates the adapter.\n997|M0 exposes only an internal semantic interface and conformance harness; a\n998|stable public SDK is deferred until tmux and one materially different backend\n999|validate the boundary.\n1000|\n1001|Manifest, Probe, Binding, and Capability Evidence IDs equal the lowercase\n1002|<code>sha256:</code> digest of RFC 8785 JCS bytes with their own ID member\n1003|omitted. A reader MUST recompute the ID before use. Manifest and Probe remain\n1004|immutable observations when later probes supersede them.\n1005|\n1006|Terminal Backend Protocol 1.0.0 has a closed request envelope containing\n1007|exactly <code>protocol</code> with literal\n1008|<code>urn:ax:protocol:terminal-backend</code>,\n1009|<code>protocol_version</code> with exact value <code>1.0.0</code>,\n1010|<code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>operation</code>, and <code>body</code>.\n1011|Its response repeats those three identity members exactly and contains\n1012|<code>ok:true,result:&lt;operation-success-body&gt;</code> or\n1013|<code>ok:false,error:StructuredError1.3</code>, never both result and error.\n1014|Operation is one of the ten names in Section 4.C and the exact bodies are its\n1015|typed matrix. Unknown members, operations, or body variants are protocol\n1016|errors. This is an AX-controlled local adapter wire, not a stable public SDK.\n1017|\n1018|AX allocates <code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>. Terminal Instance Binding\n1019|1.0.0 is the following closed immutable host-local object; no other member is\n1020|permitted:\n1021|\n1022|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1023|| --- | --- |\n1024|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding</code> |\n1025|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1026|| <code>binding_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule above |\n1027|| <code>session_id</code> | Logical Session UUIDv7 |\n1028|| <code>host_id</code> | AX Host UUIDv7 |\n1029|| <code>host_incarnation_id</code> | UUIDv7 allocated once for the current host-agent process incarnation |\n1030|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-allocated UUIDv7 |\n1031|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1032|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to admitted Manifest and Probe |\n1033|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1, equal to the Probe |\n1034|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256]; this is the canonical bound in every containing contract |\n1035|| <code>native_reference</code> | sanitized opaque string[1..512], meaningful only to this backend on this host incarnation |\n1036|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp |\n1037|| <code>supersedes_binding_id</code> | digest|null; null only for the first binding of this Session on this host incarnation |\n1038|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1039|\n1040|Identity MUST NOT be a PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token, or\n1041|mutable endpoint. Binding is host/incarnation-local and does not alter Logical\n1042|Session identity. Boundary conformance cases MUST reject generation lengths 0\n1043|and 257 and accept length 256 in the Binding, Provider Protocol 3 descriptor,\n1044|operation bodies, and CLI Result 4 summary.\n1045|\n1046|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n1047|\n1048|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n1049|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n1050|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n1051|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n1052|\n1053|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n1054|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n1055|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n1056|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n1057|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n1058|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n1059|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n1060|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n1061|\n1062|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n1063|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n1064|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1065|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n1066|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n1067|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n1068|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n1069|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n1070|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1071|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n1072|\n1073|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n1074|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n1075|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n1076|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n1077|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n1078|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n1079|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n1080|\n1081|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1082|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n1083|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1084|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n1085|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1086|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n1087|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n1088|\n1089|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n1090|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n1091|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1092|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n1093|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1094|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n1095|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n1096|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n1097|\n1098|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1099|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1100|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1101|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5f1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":339,"recorded_at":1780531400000673,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"3d40ca8e-f983-4b50-af48-a64b76836461"},"task_id":"3d40ca8e-f983-4b50-af48-a64b76836461","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"3d40ca8e-f983-4b50-af48-a64b76836461"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5f3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":340,"recorded_at":1780531400000675,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"call_id":"call_01a06f2e979d71238bf23686d827b318","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(861 line(s) above)\n862|### 4.A TerminalBackend authority and terminology\n863|\n864|TerminalBackend is a host-local presentation and delegated process-hosting\n865|module. AX alone owns Logical Session identity and lineage, Owner and AX\n866|Replica roles, leases and fencing, provider lifecycle/native identity/store,\n867|workspace materialization, Checkpoints/evidence, task-board integration, mesh\n868|replication, and takeover. A backend owns exactly one host-local\n869|<dfn>Terminal Instance</dfn>: delegated PTY/process hosting, presentation,\n870|attach/reconnect, backend-local IPC, and backend-specific process observation.\n871|\n872|An <dfn>AX Replica</dfn> is a host holding synchronized durable AX state. A\n873|<dfn>presentation replica</dfn> or <dfn>client mirror</dfn> is only a view/input\n874|client of one Terminal Instance. Presentation replication MUST NOT create an AX\n875|Replica, acquire or renew a lease, change Owner, authorize input, or publish an\n876|owner-authored event. Schemas, CLI, UI, and logs MUST NOT use these terms\n877|interchangeably.\n878|\n879|Every backend-created runtime ultimately executes exactly\n880|<code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>; a raw provider command is forbidden as a\n881|durable entry point. A backend MUST NOT interpret ownership, start or resume a\n882|provider without AX authorization, replace AX/provider/workspace/Checkpoint/\n883|task-board/mesh state, or turn attach into a lease mutation. A valid takeover\n884|or owner resume MAY bind the same Logical Session to a different conforming\n885|destination backend without clone or fork; AX emits a new immutable binding,\n886|event, and evidence and never mutates history.\n887|\n888|### 4.B Registry, identity, discovery, and trust\n889|\n890|<code>terminal_backend_id</code> is 1–128 ASCII bytes matching\n891|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:[.-][a-z0-9]+)*</code>. The <code>ax.</code> namespace is\n892|reserved. Canonical built-ins are <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n893|<code>ax.conpty</code>. Third parties use a stable vendor-owned namespace. No\n894|normative Superlogical ID is reserved.\n895|\n896|Terminal Backend Manifest 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no\n897|other member is permitted:\n898|\n899|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n900|| --- | --- |\n901|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-manifest</code> |\n902|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n903|| <code>manifest_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n904|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n905|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver |\n906|| <code>protocol_versions</code> | sorted unique semver[1..32], each in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n907|| <code>platforms</code> | sorted unique enum[1..4] from <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> |\n908|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | <code>builtin_go|local_program|trusted_executable|native_runtime</code> |\n909|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest for <code>local_program</code> or <code>trusted_executable</code>; null otherwise |\n910|| <code>static_capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] whose <code>origin</code> is <code>static</code> |\n911|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest |\n912|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code>; non-empty extensions require a later contract version |\n913|\n914|Terminal Backend Probe 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable observation; no\n915|other member is permitted:\n916|\n917|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n918|| --- | --- |\n919|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-probe</code> |\n920|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n921|| <code>probe_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n922|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n923|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to the admitted Manifest |\n924|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver selected from the Manifest's <code>protocol_versions</code> |\n925|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | enum equal to the Manifest member |\n926|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest|null exactly equal to the Manifest member |\n927|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code>, contained in the Manifest's <code>platforms</code> |\n928|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] |\n929|| <code>availability</code> | <code>available|conditional|unavailable|unknown</code> |\n930|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest of the domain-separated raw generation |\n931|| <code>capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] |\n932|| <code>evidence_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..256] referencing Capability Evidence 1.0.0 |\n933|| <code>probed_at</code> | timestamp |\n934|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n935|\n936|The generation digest uses SHA-256 over UTF-8\n937|<code>ax-terminal-backend-generation-v1\\0</code> followed by the backend's\n938|host-local raw generation bytes; it neither reveals nor reconstructs that\n939|generation. Manifest-to-Probe reconciliation is the following closed rule. The\n940|Probe <code>terminal_backend_id</code>, <code>implementation_version</code>,\n941|<code>implementation_kind</code>, and <code>executable_digest</code> MUST equal\n942|the Manifest members; its <code>protocol_version</code> MUST be exactly one member\n943|of <code>protocol_versions</code>, and its <code>platform</code> MUST be exactly\n944|one member of <code>platforms</code>. Array-to-scalar selection is membership,\n945|not aggregate equality.\n946|\n947|Let <code>M[c]</code> be the one Manifest static claim for capability\n948|<code>c</code>, when present, and <code>P[c]</code> the one Probe claim. The\n949|declared sorted-unique constraints make a duplicate key invalid before this\n950|reconciliation runs. The complete keyed relation is:\n951|\n952|1. Every <code>M[c]</code> MUST have exactly one <code>P[c]</code>; omission is a\n953|   manifest/probe mismatch.\n954|2. <code>P[c].origin=static</code> is permitted only when <code>M[c]</code>\n955|   exists, and <code>P[c]</code> MUST then equal <code>M[c]</code> member for\n956|   member. It is a static echo, not a new observation.\n957|3. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> with an existing <code>M[c]</code> is a\n958|   generation-bound override. It is permitted only when\n959|   <code>M[c].generation_variable=true</code>; its <code>value</code> MAY differ,\n960|   while <code>generation_variable</code>, <code>dependent_operations</code>, and\n961|   <code>evidence_requirements</code> MUST remain equal to <code>M[c]</code> and\n962|   the capability registry row.\n963|4. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> without <code>M[c]</code> is a probed\n964|   addition. It is permitted only for a capability in the closed registry, and\n965|   its three registry-derived members MUST equal that row. A Probe cannot add\n966|   a claim with <code>origin=static</code>.\n967|5. A true <code>P[c]</code> is admitted only when unexpired Capability Evidence\n968|   bound to this exact Manifest/Probe tuple satisfies every listed evidence\n969|   requirement. The required fact mapping is\n970|   <code>conformance_fixture-&gt;fixture_passed</code>,\n971|   <code>runtime_probe-&gt;runtime_probe_passed</code>,\n972|   <code>credential_sentinel-&gt;sentinel_passed</code>,\n973|   <code>provider_auth_smoke-&gt;provider_auth_passed</code>, and\n974|   <code>policy_authorization-&gt;policy_checked</code>. A false claim has no\n975|   matching Capability Evidence because Evidence <code>value</code> is the\n976|   literal <code>true</code>.\n977|6. <code>evidence_ids</code> MUST be exactly the sorted unique IDs of all\n978|   returned Capability Evidence objects used by true <code>P</code> claims.\n979|   Every referenced object MUST name exactly one present true claim; an ID for\n980|   an absent or false claim, an unreferenced returned object, conflicting\n981|   evidence, or duplicate/conflicting claims invalidates the whole Probe.\n982|\n983|A partial, malformed, stale, or failed Manifest, Probe, or evidence read is an\n984|error, never absence or availability. Any failed equality, membership, keyed\n985|relation, evidence binding, or evidence coverage rule is\n986|<code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code> and fails before\n987|activation; executable substitution or implementation drift additionally maps\n988|to its more specific Section 15.3 code.\n989|\n990|Discovery completes before activation. Duplicate/ambiguous IDs,\n991|manifest/probe disagreement, implementation drift, untrusted executable\n992|substitution, stale generation, unknown identity/version, or unevidenced claims\n993|fail closed. A manifest is not availability proof. External adapters use argv\n994|and local length-prefixed framing: unsigned 32-bit big-endian byte length plus\n995|UTF-8 JSON, at most 1 MiB, one request/response at a time. EOF, oversize,\n996|invalid JSON, unsolicited output, or deadline expiry terminates the adapter.\n997|M0 exposes only an internal semantic interface and conformance harness; a\n998|stable public SDK is deferred until tmux and one materially different backend\n999|validate the boundary.\n1000|\n1001|Manifest, Probe, Binding, and Capability Evidence IDs equal the lowercase\n1002|<code>sha256:</code> digest of RFC 8785 JCS bytes with their own ID member\n1003|omitted. A reader MUST recompute the ID before use. Manifest and Probe remain\n1004|immutable observations when later probes supersede them.\n1005|\n1006|Terminal Backend Protocol 1.0.0 has a closed request envelope containing\n1007|exactly <code>protocol</code> with literal\n1008|<code>urn:ax:protocol:terminal-backend</code>,\n1009|<code>protocol_version</code> with exact value <code>1.0.0</code>,\n1010|<code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>operation</code>, and <code>body</code>.\n1011|Its response repeats those three identity members exactly and contains\n1012|<code>ok:true,result:&lt;operation-success-body&gt;</code> or\n1013|<code>ok:false,error:StructuredError1.3</code>, never both result and error.\n1014|Operation is one of the ten names in Section 4.C and the exact bodies are its\n1015|typed matrix. Unknown members, operations, or body variants are protocol\n1016|errors. This is an AX-controlled local adapter wire, not a stable public SDK.\n1017|\n1018|AX allocates <code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>. Terminal Instance Binding\n1019|1.0.0 is the following closed immutable host-local object; no other member is\n1020|permitted:\n1021|\n1022|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1023|| --- | --- |\n1024|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding</code> |\n1025|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1026|| <code>binding_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule above |\n1027|| <code>session_id</code> | Logical Session UUIDv7 |\n1028|| <code>host_id</code> | AX Host UUIDv7 |\n1029|| <code>host_incarnation_id</code> | UUIDv7 allocated once for the current host-agent process incarnation |\n1030|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-allocated UUIDv7 |\n1031|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1032|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to admitted Manifest and Probe |\n1033|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1, equal to the Probe |\n1034|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256]; this is the canonical bound in every containing contract |\n1035|| <code>native_reference</code> | sanitized opaque string[1..512], meaningful only to this backend on this host incarnation |\n1036|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp |\n1037|| <code>supersedes_binding_id</code> | digest|null; null only for the first binding of this Session on this host incarnation |\n1038|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1039|\n1040|Identity MUST NOT be a PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token, or\n1041|mutable endpoint. Binding is host/incarnation-local and does not alter Logical\n1042|Session identity. Boundary conformance cases MUST reject generation lengths 0\n1043|and 257 and accept length 256 in the Binding, Provider Protocol 3 descriptor,\n1044|operation bodies, and CLI Result 4 summary.\n1045|\n1046|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n1047|\n1048|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n1049|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n1050|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n1051|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n1052|\n1053|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n1054|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n1055|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n1056|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n1057|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n1058|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n1059|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n1060|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n1061|\n1062|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n1063|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n1064|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1065|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n1066|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n1067|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n1068|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n1069|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n1070|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1071|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n1072|\n1073|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n1074|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n1075|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n1076|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n1077|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n1078|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n1079|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n1080|\n1081|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1082|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n1083|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1084|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n1085|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1086|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n1087|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n1088|\n1089|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n1090|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n1091|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1092|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n1093|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1094|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n1095|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n1096|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n1097|\n1098|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1099|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1100|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1101|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
