{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c613","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":356,"recorded_at":1780531400000707,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a2e65031-d931-4a9f-8a09-d06c31ac5c91"},"task_id":"a2e65031-d931-4a9f-8a09-d06c31ac5c91","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a2e65031-d931-4a9f-8a09-d06c31ac5c91","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(1100 line(s) above)\n1101|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1102|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1103|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1104|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n1105|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n1106|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n1107|\n1108|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1109|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1110|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1111|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1112|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1113|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1114|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1115|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1116|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n1117|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n1118|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n1119|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n1120|\n1121|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n1122|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n1123|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n1124|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n1125|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n1126|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n1127|persisted or replicated.\n1128|\n1129|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n1130|| --- | --- | --- |\n1131|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n1132|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n1133|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n1134|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n1135|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n1136|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1137|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1138|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n1139|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n1140|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n1141|\n1142|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n1143|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n1144|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n1145|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n1146|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n1147|<code>identity_match:false</code>, <code>state:absent</code>,\n1148|<code>wrapper_present:false</code>, <code>provider_present:null</code>,\n1149|<code>attachable:false</code>, and both last fields null; it does not authorize\n1150|fallback. <code>provider_present</code> is null unless provider observation was\n1151|requested and evidenced. <code>attachable</code> is true only in\n1152|<code>parked|active</code> with a currently evidenced matching attach\n1153|capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the\n1154|request and AttachAuthorization; <code>attach_descriptor</code> in\n1155|<code>create</code> is non-null exactly when <code>interactive</code> is true.\n1156|\n1157|The following table is the exact transition, authorization, idempotency,\n1158|deadline/recovery, evidence, capability, and Structured Error 1.3 mapping.\n1159|An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\n1160|syntactically valid request; AX-local parsing may additionally emit\n1161|<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\n1162|transition and no side effect.\n1163|\n1164|| Operation | Allowed source → success state; exact side effects | Authorization and idempotency key | Deadline/lost-result recovery and required evidence | Capability dependencies | Allowed error codes |\n1165|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1166|| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1167|| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1168|| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1169|| <code>attach</code> | <code>parked</code> → <code>active</code> or <code>active</code> → <code>active</code>; <code>attach_client_created</code> | valid unexpired AttachAuthorization equal to request transport/input; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/\" + client_id</code> | timeout creates no authorized input unless the durable client receipt says so; retry same client ID; attach-policy/capability evidence | matching <code>local_attach|remote_attach|web_attach</code>; <code>multi_attach</code> for overlap; <code>multiple_input_clients</code> plus AX policy for concurrent input | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1170|| <code>status</code> | <code>absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → same state; none | none; key is full queried identity tuple | timeout/read failure is unknown, never absent; retry query; status evidence IDs only | <code>provider_process_observation</code> exactly when provider observation requested | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1171|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>active|parked</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>input_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation</code> | receipt precedes input closure; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; evidence binds closure time/generation | <code>input_quiescence</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1172|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>safe_boundary_observed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind</code> | lesser of request deadline and timeout; identical retry returns the same proof; no proof on timeout; safe-boundary evidence | <code>safe_boundary_observation</code>; also <code>provider_process_observation</code> for provider proof kinds | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1173|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>graceful_stop_requested,process_closed,backend_store_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id</code> | lesser deadline/timeout; lost result requires <code>status</code>, then same-key retry only if not closed; boundary and closure evidence | <code>graceful_stop</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1174|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>stale_incarnation_terminated,process_closed</code> | <code>force_stale</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/terminate/\" + stale_lease_id + \"/\" + decimal(stale_epoch)</code> | deadline may leave uncertain closure; use <code>status</code> before same-key retry; diagnostic, fencing, and closure evidence | <code>stale_process_termination</code> and <code>provider_process_observation</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1175|| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1176|\n1177|Create is idempotent on <code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code> across\n1178|controller crash and lost result. AX and backend durably bind the pair before\n1179|the first child side effect. Identical retry returns the one result/instance;\n1180|a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n1181|Only a successful status read proves absence. Attach is ownership-observational\n1182|for current-owner resume, local/remote/web, reconnect, and multi-attach.\n1183|\n1184|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n1185|\n1186|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\n1187|<dfn>TerminalBackendOperation</dfn> is exactly\n1188|<code>manifest|probe|create|attach|status|quiesce-input|wait-safe-boundary|request-stop|terminate-stale|restore</code>.\n1189|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceRequirement</dfn> is exactly\n1190|<code>conformance_fixture|runtime_probe|credential_sentinel|provider_auth_smoke|policy_authorization</code>.\n1191|\n1192|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1193|<code>capability:TerminalBackendCapability</code>,\n1194|<code>origin:static|probed</code>, <code>value:boolean</code>,\n1195|<code>generation_variable:boolean</code>,\n1196|<code>dependent_operations:sorted-unique TerminalBackendOperation[1..10]</code>,\n1197|and <code>evidence_requirements:sorted-unique CapabilityEvidenceRequirement[1..5]</code>.\n1198|The latter three members MUST exactly equal the registry row for the capability;\n1199|a Manifest or Probe cannot redefine them. A false claim is retained to make a\n1200|probed refusal explicit but confers no operation.\n1201|\n1202|| Capability | Exact semantics | Generation-variable | Exact dependent operations | Exact evidence requirements |\n1203|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1204|| <code>durable_disconnect</code> | Wrapper survives every client disconnect. | false | <code>create,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1205|| <code>local_attach</code> | Local-only presentation. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1206|| <code>remote_attach</code> | Presentation over trusted private mesh only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1207|| <code>web_attach</code> | Web presentation over an admitted transport only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1208|| <code>multi_attach</code> | Concurrent presentation clients; no multi-input or ownership implication. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1209|| <code>headless_creation</code> | Create without UI or prompt in the proven execution realm. | true | <code>create</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1210|| <code>reboot_restoration</code> | Re-establish after reboot; does not claim process survival. | true | <code>restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1211|| <code>input_quiescence</code> | Reject new input with generation-bound evidence. | true | <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1212|| <code>safe_boundary_observation</code> | Observe AX/provider-selected safe-boundary proof. | true | <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1213|| <code>provider_process_observation</code> | Observe provider presence without PID identity. | true | <code>status,terminate-stale,wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1214|| <code>graceful_stop</code> | Request and observe orderly exit. | true | <code>request-stop</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1215|| <code>stale_process_termination</code> | Target one fenced stale incarnation. | true | <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1216|| <code>terminal_state_retention</code> | Retain local presentation state, never portable Checkpoint state. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1217|| <code>scrollback_retention</code> | Retain local scrollback, never replicated terminal output. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1218|| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\n1219|| <code>multiple_input_clients</code> | Backend serializes multiple input clients; AX policy separately authorizes use. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1220|\n1221|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceFact</dfn> is the exact enum\n1222|<code>fixture_passed|runtime_probe_passed|sentinel_passed|provider_auth_passed|policy_checked|ui_absent|prompt_absent</code>.\n1223|Capability Evidence 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no other\n1224|member is permitted:\n1225|\n1226|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1227|| --- | --- |\n1228|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence</code> |\n1229|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1230|| <code>evidence_id</code> | digest computed by the Section 4.B identity rule |\n1231|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1232|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to Manifest and Probe |\n1233|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver equal to Probe |\n1234|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest equal to Probe |\n1235|| <code>capability</code> | TerminalBackendCapability |\n1236|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n1237|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n1238|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n1239|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n1240|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n1241|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n1242|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n1243|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n1244|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n1245|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n1246|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1247|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1248|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1249|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1250|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1251|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1252|\n1253|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n1254|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n1255|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n1256|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n1257|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n1258|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n1259|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n1260|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n1261|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n1262|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n1263|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n1264|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n1265|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n1266|change and before activation.\n1267|\n1268|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n1269|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n1270|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n1271|activation when policy allows.\n1272|\n1273|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n1274|\n1275|| Classification | Members and rule |\n1276|| --- | --- |\n1277|| Safe immutable evidence | Sanitized backend identity/version/platform/conformance/capability evidence; MAY persist and replicate after validation. |\n1278|| Host-local durable metadata | Instance/binding IDs, sanitized native reference, generation, idempotency receipt, last effect; host-local, non-replicable. |\n1279|| Derived cache | Discovery/availability/attachability/process observations and probe views; rebuildable, non-authoritative. |\n1280|| Sensitive runtime state | IPC, tmux sockets, named pipes, attach/relay credentials, backend auth/live databases, GUI/login attestations, provider credentials; owner-only and non-replicable. |\n1281|| Forbidden | Raw native reference, PID/handle, endpoint/token, terminal output/scrollback, unrestricted environment, credential detail, and live-process facts MUST NOT replicate. |\n1282|\n1283|Presentation transport is exactly <code>local_only</code>,\n1284|<code>trusted_private_mesh</code>, or <code>third_party_relay</code>. Current AX\n1285|admits only the first two. A relay-required/public-service backend is unavailable\n1286|pending explicit future product/contract approval. AX retains no permanent\n1287|public TCP listener. Attach transport carries no AX authoritative state,\n1288|provider store, workspace, Checkpoint, task-board data, or ownership change.\n1289|\n1290|The exact v0.4.3 Configuration 1/2 <code>tmux|conpty</code>, Provider Protocol 2\n1291|TerminalDescriptor, Session Event 1 terminal payloads, and CLI Result 1 start/\n1292|resume shapes and digests remain immutable. Version adapters deterministically\n1293|map legacy <code>tmux</code> to <code>ax.tmux</code> and <code>conpty</code> to\n1294|<code>ax.conpty</code>, with version/generation <code>legacy_unreported</code>\n1295|and no inferred capabilities. Reverse projection exists only for those two IDs;\n1296|other IDs return <code>incompatible_schema</code>, never fallback. Translation\n1297|never rewrites or re-digests history.\n1298|\n1299|New readers accept old objects through the adapter. Old readers may browse/sync\n1300|opaque newer immutable records but cannot activate, restore, or write them.\n1301|Mixed peers negotiate each containing contract independently; no common backend\n1302|major means browse/sync only. Unknown/unsupported IDs remain visible as unknown/\n1303|unavailable; registry read failure is never absence. Lower-version writers are\n1304|read-only and cannot write downgrade replacements. Bootstrap permits only a\n1305|framed <code>manifest</code> call in an understood major. Capability negotiation\n1306|is the intersection plus valid bound evidence, never union or inference.\n1307|\n1308|Mesh RPC 4.0.0 is defined normatively in Section 11.9: its exact 25-key hello\n1309|map changes the RPC and Session Event arrays and adds exactly\n1310|<code>terminal_backend_evidence=[\"1.0.0\"]</code>; its exact eighth namespace\n1311|contains only sanitized Manifest, Probe, and Capability Evidence objects.\n1312|Terminal Instance Binding remains host-local durable metadata and is not a\n1313|namespace member; replicated Session Events carry only its digest as an opaque\n1314|audit reference. RPC 2/3 peers report this namespace unsupported, never empty.\n1315|\n1316|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 and its exact TerminalDescriptor are defined in\n1317|Section 7.A. Session Event 4.0.0 and its exact\n1318|<code>terminal.created</code>/<code>session.resumed</code> payloads are defined\n1319|in Section 5.2; neither payload contains a Terminal Instance ID, backend\n1320|generation, or native reference. CLI Result 4.0.0 local inspection and\n1321|start/resume bodies are defined in Section 14.6. Structured Error 1.3.0 literal\n1322|codes, exit classes, and bootstrap behavior are defined in Section 15.3. These\n1323|canonical definitions, not this compatibility summary, determine their closed\n1324|shapes.\n1325|\n1326|**Future candidate (non-normative; unavailable): Superlogical.** Dated public\n1327|sources retrieved 2026-08-29 describe planned reconnect/share, web/native\n1328|clients, software-driven structured actions, and libghostty use; the official\n1329|GitHub organization exposed no public repositories that day. They establish no\n1330|public release, AX adapter, API/SDK/protocol, backend ID/version, capability\n1331|evidence, lifecycle, ownership, security, or replication contract. The label\n1332|enables nothing. Admission requires dated evidence for create, attach/reconnect,\n1333|status/generation, quiescence, graceful/stale stop, restore, exact\n1334|<code>ax pane</code>, headless automation, credential proof, transport/auth,\n1335|no AX ownership/authoritative-state transfer, and crash/security/conformance\n1336|negative tests.\n1337|\n1338|### 4.1 Terminal backend interface\n1339|\n1340|Every terminal backend MUST implement these semantic operations:\n1341|\n1342|| Operation | Required result |\n1343|| --- | --- |\n1344|| <code>create</code> | With <code>session_id</code> and caller-stable <code>bootstrap_operation_id</code>, create a durable pane/process whose only stable entry point is <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>. |\n1345|| <code>attach</code> | Connect an operator to the local terminal without changing ownership. |\n1346|| <code>status</code> | Report process presence, wrapper state, provider child state, and attachability. |\n1347|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | Stop new operator/provider input while retaining observation. |\n1348|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | Prove the adapter-specific safe boundary or time out. |\n1349|| <code>request-stop</code> | Ask the provider to exit through a version-tested graceful path. |\n1350|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | Terminate a process only for explicit force recovery after preserving diagnostics. |\n1351|| <code>restore</code> | Recreate the wrapper after reboot and consult current ownership before any provider resume. |\n1352|\n1353|The wrapper MUST validate configuration, load the logical session, synchronize\n1354|known lease records when possible, and compare the local fencing token before\n1355|launching a provider. It MUST park safely when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n1356|or unverified.\n1357|\n1358|Terminal creation and the wrapper's first child start are idempotent on\n1359|<code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code>. The backend MUST durably bind\n1360|that pair before child creation. An identical retry returns or reattaches to\n1361|the one recorded wrapper/child; changing the operation for a session still in\n1362|the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. After a lost result,\n1363|<code>status</code> plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one\n1364|child before any start retry. This contract never persists or replicates a PID\n1365|as identity.\n1366|\n1367|### 4.2 tmux backend\n1368|\n1369|On macOS, Linux, and WSL2, the supported durable terminal backend is tmux. Every\n1370|managed pane MUST run:\n1371|\n1372|~~~shell\n1373|ax pane <logical-session-id>\n1374|~~~\n1375|\n1376|It MUST NOT run the raw provider command as the pane's stable command.\n1377|<code>tmux-resurrect</code> plus <code>tmux-continuum</code> MAY recreate local\n1378|tmux layout and invoke the wrapper after reboot. They MUST NOT be described or\n1379|used as cross-host migration.\n1380|\n1381|AX MUST use its dedicated <code>-S</code> server and MUST NOT discover or reuse\n1382|the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name. On macOS, server\n1383|creation is credential-sensitive. A Background caller MUST NOT create a\n1384|credential-dependent tmux server. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon,\n1385|or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and\n1386|its attested AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return\n1387|<code>capability_unavailable</code> with typed realm/readiness details and MUST\n1388|NOT fall back to direct server creation.\n1389|\n1390|<code>launchctl managername</code> is a diagnostic hint only. Conformance\n1391|requires a functional AX sentinel inside the exact tmux server plus a separate\n1392|provider-auth smoke using the selected provider. Evidence MUST bind the exact\n1393|tmux server generation, provider build, and macOS version. Aqua alone and\n1394|sentinel-only evidence are insufficient. Any provider flow requiring GUI\n1395|interaction, Keychain UI, a permission prompt, or other human action fails\n1396|closed until that interaction succeeds in the verified GUI realm.\n1397|\n1398|After restore, the wrapper MUST:\n1399|\n1400|1. read the latest locally known lease;\n1401|2. attempt a mesh lease refresh without blocking forever;\n1402|3. resume locally only if the local host has the winning lease and the required\n1403|   materialization is valid;\n1404|4. offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session in an\n1405|   interactive terminal; or\n1406|5. enter <code>parked</code> without launching the provider in all other cases.\n1407|\n1408|Logout or reboot invalidates unrenewed realm evidence. Without a verified GUI\n1409|realm, recovery MUST remain parked until GUI login re-establishes the broker,\n1410|functional sentinel, provider-auth smoke, and their generation/build/version\n1411|binding. A cached sentinel or prior <code>managername</code> observation MUST\n1412|NOT authorize resume.\n1413|\n1414|### 4.3 Native Windows backend\n1415|\n1416|Native Windows PowerShell MUST use a Windows terminal backend implemented with\n1417|Go process supervision and ConPTY. It MUST support mesh sync, workspace and\n1418|provider materialization, direct/provider resume, task-board open/adopt, remote\n1419|attach, graceful takeover when the provider row passes ConPTY gates, force\n1420|takeover, stop, and continuation.\n1421|\n1422|Native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux or tmux resurrection. A reboot destroys the\n1423|live ConPTY. The user service MUST recreate <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>,\n1424|which resumes from the latest valid checkpoint only after lease validation.\n1425|Terminal scrollback and live process memory are not portable state.\n1426|\n1427|Full tmux restore on a Windows computer is a WSL2 feature and uses the Linux\n1428|paths, process model, and provider installation inside that distribution. A\n1429|native Windows provider store and a WSL2 provider store are distinct\n1430|materialization targets.\n1431|\n1432|### 4.4 User services\n1433|\n1434|The background service integration is:\n1435|\n1436|- a launchd agent on macOS;\n1437|- a systemd user unit on Linux and WSL2 where systemd is enabled;\n1438|- otherwise an explicitly installed per-user periodic launcher on WSL2; and\n1439|- a Scheduled Task or per-user service on native Windows.\n1440|\n1441|The service MAY run periodic sync, peer health checks, tombstone\n1442|acknowledgement, stale-process detection, and wrapper restoration. Core commands\n1443|MUST work without it. Service absence MUST degrade freshness, not corrupt\n1444|ownership.\n1445|\n1446|The macOS launchd background control plane and Aqua terminal broker are separate\n1447|roles. The control plane MUST NOT acquire GUI/Keychain authority by proxy and\n1448|MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server. The Aqua broker exposes\n1449|only authenticated, same-user, generation-bound terminal readiness and server\n1450|operations; it does not gain lease, workspace, provider, or replication\n1451|authority.\n1452|\n1453|## 5. Domain records and state machine\n1454|\n1455|### 5.1 Session Record\n1456|\n1457|This subsection defines the immutable Session Record <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1458|variant. It is created exactly once and uses schema\n1459|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-record</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1460|5.1.1 and 5.1.2 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c615","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":357,"recorded_at":1780531400000709,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a2e65031-d931-4a9f-8a09-d06c31ac5c91"},"task_id":"a2e65031-d931-4a9f-8a09-d06c31ac5c91","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"a2e65031-d931-4a9f-8a09-d06c31ac5c91"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c617","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":358,"recorded_at":1780531400000711,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"call_id":"call_01a06f2ea51f78f1a860b1ab4b21b6ca","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(1100 line(s) above)\n1101|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1102|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1103|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1104|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n1105|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n1106|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n1107|\n1108|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1109|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1110|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1111|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1112|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1113|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1114|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1115|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1116|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n1117|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n1118|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n1119|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n1120|\n1121|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n1122|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n1123|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n1124|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n1125|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n1126|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n1127|persisted or replicated.\n1128|\n1129|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n1130|| --- | --- | --- |\n1131|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n1132|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n1133|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n1134|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n1135|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n1136|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1137|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1138|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n1139|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n1140|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n1141|\n1142|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n1143|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n1144|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n1145|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n1146|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n1147|<code>identity_match:false</code>, <code>state:absent</code>,\n1148|<code>wrapper_present:false</code>, <code>provider_present:null</code>,\n1149|<code>attachable:false</code>, and both last fields null; it does not authorize\n1150|fallback. <code>provider_present</code> is null unless provider observation was\n1151|requested and evidenced. <code>attachable</code> is true only in\n1152|<code>parked|active</code> with a currently evidenced matching attach\n1153|capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the\n1154|request and AttachAuthorization; <code>attach_descriptor</code> in\n1155|<code>create</code> is non-null exactly when <code>interactive</code> is true.\n1156|\n1157|The following table is the exact transition, authorization, idempotency,\n1158|deadline/recovery, evidence, capability, and Structured Error 1.3 mapping.\n1159|An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\n1160|syntactically valid request; AX-local parsing may additionally emit\n1161|<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\n1162|transition and no side effect.\n1163|\n1164|| Operation | Allowed source → success state; exact side effects | Authorization and idempotency key | Deadline/lost-result recovery and required evidence | Capability dependencies | Allowed error codes |\n1165|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1166|| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1167|| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1168|| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1169|| <code>attach</code> | <code>parked</code> → <code>active</code> or <code>active</code> → <code>active</code>; <code>attach_client_created</code> | valid unexpired AttachAuthorization equal to request transport/input; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/\" + client_id</code> | timeout creates no authorized input unless the durable client receipt says so; retry same client ID; attach-policy/capability evidence | matching <code>local_attach|remote_attach|web_attach</code>; <code>multi_attach</code> for overlap; <code>multiple_input_clients</code> plus AX policy for concurrent input | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1170|| <code>status</code> | <code>absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → same state; none | none; key is full queried identity tuple | timeout/read failure is unknown, never absent; retry query; status evidence IDs only | <code>provider_process_observation</code> exactly when provider observation requested | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1171|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>active|parked</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>input_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation</code> | receipt precedes input closure; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; evidence binds closure time/generation | <code>input_quiescence</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1172|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>safe_boundary_observed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind</code> | lesser of request deadline and timeout; identical retry returns the same proof; no proof on timeout; safe-boundary evidence | <code>safe_boundary_observation</code>; also <code>provider_process_observation</code> for provider proof kinds | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1173|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>graceful_stop_requested,process_closed,backend_store_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id</code> | lesser deadline/timeout; lost result requires <code>status</code>, then same-key retry only if not closed; boundary and closure evidence | <code>graceful_stop</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1174|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>stale_incarnation_terminated,process_closed</code> | <code>force_stale</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/terminate/\" + stale_lease_id + \"/\" + decimal(stale_epoch)</code> | deadline may leave uncertain closure; use <code>status</code> before same-key retry; diagnostic, fencing, and closure evidence | <code>stale_process_termination</code> and <code>provider_process_observation</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1175|| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1176|\n1177|Create is idempotent on <code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code> across\n1178|controller crash and lost result. AX and backend durably bind the pair before\n1179|the first child side effect. Identical retry returns the one result/instance;\n1180|a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n1181|Only a successful status read proves absence. Attach is ownership-observational\n1182|for current-owner resume, local/remote/web, reconnect, and multi-attach.\n1183|\n1184|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n1185|\n1186|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\n1187|<dfn>TerminalBackendOperation</dfn> is exactly\n1188|<code>manifest|probe|create|attach|status|quiesce-input|wait-safe-boundary|request-stop|terminate-stale|restore</code>.\n1189|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceRequirement</dfn> is exactly\n1190|<code>conformance_fixture|runtime_probe|credential_sentinel|provider_auth_smoke|policy_authorization</code>.\n1191|\n1192|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1193|<code>capability:TerminalBackendCapability</code>,\n1194|<code>origin:static|probed</code>, <code>value:boolean</code>,\n1195|<code>generation_variable:boolean</code>,\n1196|<code>dependent_operations:sorted-unique TerminalBackendOperation[1..10]</code>,\n1197|and <code>evidence_requirements:sorted-unique CapabilityEvidenceRequirement[1..5]</code>.\n1198|The latter three members MUST exactly equal the registry row for the capability;\n1199|a Manifest or Probe cannot redefine them. A false claim is retained to make a\n1200|probed refusal explicit but confers no operation.\n1201|\n1202|| Capability | Exact semantics | Generation-variable | Exact dependent operations | Exact evidence requirements |\n1203|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1204|| <code>durable_disconnect</code> | Wrapper survives every client disconnect. | false | <code>create,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1205|| <code>local_attach</code> | Local-only presentation. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1206|| <code>remote_attach</code> | Presentation over trusted private mesh only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1207|| <code>web_attach</code> | Web presentation over an admitted transport only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1208|| <code>multi_attach</code> | Concurrent presentation clients; no multi-input or ownership implication. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1209|| <code>headless_creation</code> | Create without UI or prompt in the proven execution realm. | true | <code>create</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1210|| <code>reboot_restoration</code> | Re-establish after reboot; does not claim process survival. | true | <code>restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1211|| <code>input_quiescence</code> | Reject new input with generation-bound evidence. | true | <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1212|| <code>safe_boundary_observation</code> | Observe AX/provider-selected safe-boundary proof. | true | <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1213|| <code>provider_process_observation</code> | Observe provider presence without PID identity. | true | <code>status,terminate-stale,wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1214|| <code>graceful_stop</code> | Request and observe orderly exit. | true | <code>request-stop</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1215|| <code>stale_process_termination</code> | Target one fenced stale incarnation. | true | <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1216|| <code>terminal_state_retention</code> | Retain local presentation state, never portable Checkpoint state. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1217|| <code>scrollback_retention</code> | Retain local scrollback, never replicated terminal output. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1218|| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\n1219|| <code>multiple_input_clients</code> | Backend serializes multiple input clients; AX policy separately authorizes use. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1220|\n1221|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceFact</dfn> is the exact enum\n1222|<code>fixture_passed|runtime_probe_passed|sentinel_passed|provider_auth_passed|policy_checked|ui_absent|prompt_absent</code>.\n1223|Capability Evidence 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no other\n1224|member is permitted:\n1225|\n1226|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1227|| --- | --- |\n1228|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence</code> |\n1229|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1230|| <code>evidence_id</code> | digest computed by the Section 4.B identity rule |\n1231|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1232|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to Manifest and Probe |\n1233|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver equal to Probe |\n1234|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest equal to Probe |\n1235|| <code>capability</code> | TerminalBackendCapability |\n1236|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n1237|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n1238|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n1239|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n1240|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n1241|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n1242|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n1243|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n1244|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n1245|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n1246|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1247|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1248|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1249|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1250|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1251|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1252|\n1253|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n1254|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n1255|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n1256|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n1257|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n1258|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n1259|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n1260|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n1261|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n1262|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n1263|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n1264|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n1265|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n1266|change and before activation.\n1267|\n1268|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n1269|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n1270|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n1271|activation when policy allows.\n1272|\n1273|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n1274|\n1275|| Classification | Members and rule |\n1276|| --- | --- |\n1277|| Safe immutable evidence | Sanitized backend identity/version/platform/conformance/capability evidence; MAY persist and replicate after validation. |\n1278|| Host-local durable metadata | Instance/binding IDs, sanitized native reference, generation, idempotency receipt, last effect; host-local, non-replicable. |\n1279|| Derived cache | Discovery/availability/attachability/process observations and probe views; rebuildable, non-authoritative. |\n1280|| Sensitive runtime state | IPC, tmux sockets, named pipes, attach/relay credentials, backend auth/live databases, GUI/login attestations, provider credentials; owner-only and non-replicable. |\n1281|| Forbidden | Raw native reference, PID/handle, endpoint/token, terminal output/scrollback, unrestricted environment, credential detail, and live-process facts MUST NOT replicate. |\n1282|\n1283|Presentation transport is exactly <code>local_only</code>,\n1284|<code>trusted_private_mesh</code>, or <code>third_party_relay</code>. Current AX\n1285|admits only the first two. A relay-required/public-service backend is unavailable\n1286|pending explicit future product/contract approval. AX retains no permanent\n1287|public TCP listener. Attach transport carries no AX authoritative state,\n1288|provider store, workspace, Checkpoint, task-board data, or ownership change.\n1289|\n1290|The exact v0.4.3 Configuration 1/2 <code>tmux|conpty</code>, Provider Protocol 2\n1291|TerminalDescriptor, Session Event 1 terminal payloads, and CLI Result 1 start/\n1292|resume shapes and digests remain immutable. Version adapters deterministically\n1293|map legacy <code>tmux</code> to <code>ax.tmux</code> and <code>conpty</code> to\n1294|<code>ax.conpty</code>, with version/generation <code>legacy_unreported</code>\n1295|and no inferred capabilities. Reverse projection exists only for those two IDs;\n1296|other IDs return <code>incompatible_schema</code>, never fallback. Translation\n1297|never rewrites or re-digests history.\n1298|\n1299|New readers accept old objects through the adapter. Old readers may browse/sync\n1300|opaque newer immutable records but cannot activate, restore, or write them.\n1301|Mixed peers negotiate each containing contract independently; no common backend\n1302|major means browse/sync only. Unknown/unsupported IDs remain visible as unknown/\n1303|unavailable; registry read failure is never absence. Lower-version writers are\n1304|read-only and cannot write downgrade replacements. Bootstrap permits only a\n1305|framed <code>manifest</code> call in an understood major. Capability negotiation\n1306|is the intersection plus valid bound evidence, never union or inference.\n1307|\n1308|Mesh RPC 4.0.0 is defined normatively in Section 11.9: its exact 25-key hello\n1309|map changes the RPC and Session Event arrays and adds exactly\n1310|<code>terminal_backend_evidence=[\"1.0.0\"]</code>; its exact eighth namespace\n1311|contains only sanitized Manifest, Probe, and Capability Evidence objects.\n1312|Terminal Instance Binding remains host-local durable metadata and is not a\n1313|namespace member; replicated Session Events carry only its digest as an opaque\n1314|audit reference. RPC 2/3 peers report this namespace unsupported, never empty.\n1315|\n1316|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 and its exact TerminalDescriptor are defined in\n1317|Section 7.A. Session Event 4.0.0 and its exact\n1318|<code>terminal.created</code>/<code>session.resumed</code> payloads are defined\n1319|in Section 5.2; neither payload contains a Terminal Instance ID, backend\n1320|generation, or native reference. CLI Result 4.0.0 local inspection and\n1321|start/resume bodies are defined in Section 14.6. Structured Error 1.3.0 literal\n1322|codes, exit classes, and bootstrap behavior are defined in Section 15.3. These\n1323|canonical definitions, not this compatibility summary, determine their closed\n1324|shapes.\n1325|\n1326|**Future candidate (non-normative; unavailable): Superlogical.** Dated public\n1327|sources retrieved 2026-08-29 describe planned reconnect/share, web/native\n1328|clients, software-driven structured actions, and libghostty use; the official\n1329|GitHub organization exposed no public repositories that day. They establish no\n1330|public release, AX adapter, API/SDK/protocol, backend ID/version, capability\n1331|evidence, lifecycle, ownership, security, or replication contract. The label\n1332|enables nothing. Admission requires dated evidence for create, attach/reconnect,\n1333|status/generation, quiescence, graceful/stale stop, restore, exact\n1334|<code>ax pane</code>, headless automation, credential proof, transport/auth,\n1335|no AX ownership/authoritative-state transfer, and crash/security/conformance\n1336|negative tests.\n1337|\n1338|### 4.1 Terminal backend interface\n1339|\n1340|Every terminal backend MUST implement these semantic operations:\n1341|\n1342|| Operation | Required result |\n1343|| --- | --- |\n1344|| <code>create</code> | With <code>session_id</code> and caller-stable <code>bootstrap_operation_id</code>, create a durable pane/process whose only stable entry point is <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>. |\n1345|| <code>attach</code> | Connect an operator to the local terminal without changing ownership. |\n1346|| <code>status</code> | Report process presence, wrapper state, provider child state, and attachability. |\n1347|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | Stop new operator/provider input while retaining observation. |\n1348|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | Prove the adapter-specific safe boundary or time out. |\n1349|| <code>request-stop</code> | Ask the provider to exit through a version-tested graceful path. |\n1350|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | Terminate a process only for explicit force recovery after preserving diagnostics. |\n1351|| <code>restore</code> | Recreate the wrapper after reboot and consult current ownership before any provider resume. |\n1352|\n1353|The wrapper MUST validate configuration, load the logical session, synchronize\n1354|known lease records when possible, and compare the local fencing token before\n1355|launching a provider. It MUST park safely when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n1356|or unverified.\n1357|\n1358|Terminal creation and the wrapper's first child start are idempotent on\n1359|<code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code>. The backend MUST durably bind\n1360|that pair before child creation. An identical retry returns or reattaches to\n1361|the one recorded wrapper/child; changing the operation for a session still in\n1362|the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. After a lost result,\n1363|<code>status</code> plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one\n1364|child before any start retry. This contract never persists or replicates a PID\n1365|as identity.\n1366|\n1367|### 4.2 tmux backend\n1368|\n1369|On macOS, Linux, and WSL2, the supported durable terminal backend is tmux. Every\n1370|managed pane MUST run:\n1371|\n1372|~~~shell\n1373|ax pane <logical-session-id>\n1374|~~~\n1375|\n1376|It MUST NOT run the raw provider command as the pane's stable command.\n1377|<code>tmux-resurrect</code> plus <code>tmux-continuum</code> MAY recreate local\n1378|tmux layout and invoke the wrapper after reboot. They MUST NOT be described or\n1379|used as cross-host migration.\n1380|\n1381|AX MUST use its dedicated <code>-S</code> server and MUST NOT discover or reuse\n1382|the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name. On macOS, server\n1383|creation is credential-sensitive. A Background caller MUST NOT create a\n1384|credential-dependent tmux server. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon,\n1385|or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and\n1386|its attested AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return\n1387|<code>capability_unavailable</code> with typed realm/readiness details and MUST\n1388|NOT fall back to direct server creation.\n1389|\n1390|<code>launchctl managername</code> is a diagnostic hint only. Conformance\n1391|requires a functional AX sentinel inside the exact tmux server plus a separate\n1392|provider-auth smoke using the selected provider. Evidence MUST bind the exact\n1393|tmux server generation, provider build, and macOS version. Aqua alone and\n1394|sentinel-only evidence are insufficient. Any provider flow requiring GUI\n1395|interaction, Keychain UI, a permission prompt, or other human action fails\n1396|closed until that interaction succeeds in the verified GUI realm.\n1397|\n1398|After restore, the wrapper MUST:\n1399|\n1400|1. read the latest locally known lease;\n1401|2. attempt a mesh lease refresh without blocking forever;\n1402|3. resume locally only if the local host has the winning lease and the required\n1403|   materialization is valid;\n1404|4. offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session in an\n1405|   interactive terminal; or\n1406|5. enter <code>parked</code> without launching the provider in all other cases.\n1407|\n1408|Logout or reboot invalidates unrenewed realm evidence. Without a verified GUI\n1409|realm, recovery MUST remain parked until GUI login re-establishes the broker,\n1410|functional sentinel, provider-auth smoke, and their generation/build/version\n1411|binding. A cached sentinel or prior <code>managername</code> observation MUST\n1412|NOT authorize resume.\n1413|\n1414|### 4.3 Native Windows backend\n1415|\n1416|Native Windows PowerShell MUST use a Windows terminal backend implemented with\n1417|Go process supervision and ConPTY. It MUST support mesh sync, workspace and\n1418|provider materialization, direct/provider resume, task-board open/adopt, remote\n1419|attach, graceful takeover when the provider row passes ConPTY gates, force\n1420|takeover, stop, and continuation.\n1421|\n1422|Native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux or tmux resurrection. A reboot destroys the\n1423|live ConPTY. The user service MUST recreate <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>,\n1424|which resumes from the latest valid checkpoint only after lease validation.\n1425|Terminal scrollback and live process memory are not portable state.\n1426|\n1427|Full tmux restore on a Windows computer is a WSL2 feature and uses the Linux\n1428|paths, process model, and provider installation inside that distribution. A\n1429|native Windows provider store and a WSL2 provider store are distinct\n1430|materialization targets.\n1431|\n1432|### 4.4 User services\n1433|\n1434|The background service integration is:\n1435|\n1436|- a launchd agent on macOS;\n1437|- a systemd user unit on Linux and WSL2 where systemd is enabled;\n1438|- otherwise an explicitly installed per-user periodic launcher on WSL2; and\n1439|- a Scheduled Task or per-user service on native Windows.\n1440|\n1441|The service MAY run periodic sync, peer health checks, tombstone\n1442|acknowledgement, stale-process detection, and wrapper restoration. Core commands\n1443|MUST work without it. Service absence MUST degrade freshness, not corrupt\n1444|ownership.\n1445|\n1446|The macOS launchd background control plane and Aqua terminal broker are separate\n1447|roles. The control plane MUST NOT acquire GUI/Keychain authority by proxy and\n1448|MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server. The Aqua broker exposes\n1449|only authenticated, same-user, generation-bound terminal readiness and server\n1450|operations; it does not gain lease, workspace, provider, or replication\n1451|authority.\n1452|\n1453|## 5. Domain records and state machine\n1454|\n1455|### 5.1 Session Record\n1456|\n1457|This subsection defines the immutable Session Record <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1458|variant. It is created exactly once and uses schema\n1459|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-record</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1460|5.1.1 and 5.1.2 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
