{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c637","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":374,"recorded_at":1780531400000743,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"110a6f93-f97f-4153-a0a9-e5b31f40587c"},"task_id":"110a6f93-f97f-4153-a0a9-e5b31f40587c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"110a6f93-f97f-4153-a0a9-e5b31f40587c","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-14-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"6\\\\.5\\\\|7\\\\.A\\\\|TerminalDescriptor\\\\|Configuration 3\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.md | head -n 30\",\n  \"description\": \"Locate sections 6.5 and 7.A\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"1291:TerminalDescriptor, Session Event 1 terminal payloads, and CLI Result 1 start/\\n1316:Provider Protocol 3.0.0 and its exact TerminalDescriptor are defined in\\n1317:Section 7.A. Session Event 4.0.0 and its exact\\n2575:### 6.5 Configuration 3.0.0 TerminalBackend extension\\n2577:Configuration 3.0.0 retains every v2 member and replaces only the closed\\n2888:| <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>interactive:boolean</code>, <code>columns:uint16[1..1000]</code>, <code>rows:uint16[1..1000]</code> |\\n3074:| <code>launch</code> | <code>{session_record:Session Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, launch_plan:Launch Plan, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\\n3076:| <code>quiesce</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{proof:SafeBoundaryProof}</code> |\\n3083:| <code>resume</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\\n3084:| <code>fork</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, source_identity:Provider Identity Record, source_checkpoint:Checkpoint Record, new_session_record:Session Record, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, result_kind:native_fork&#124;supported_import, planned_native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null, spawn_plan:SpawnPlan, requires_provider_materialization:boolean, provenance_verified:boolean}</code> |\\n3085:| <code>stop</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, mode:graceful&#124;force, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{closure:ProcessClosure}</code> |\\n3452:### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\\n3456:except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\\n10273:<code>terminal.backend.doctor</code>. They are read-only and obey Sections 6.5\\n11304:executable requires the closed Configuration 3 trust tuple and an exact\\n11320:### 16.5 Force-takeover risk\\n12141:| Attach, takeover, failure, and fork | Sections 5.3–5.7, 13, 14, 15, 16.5, 19.4 |\\n12308:| First-class registry, identity, versions, discovery, trust, and conformance | Sections 4.B, 6.5, 7.A, 15.3, and Appendix D define closed IDs, AX-reserved built-ins, manifest/probe agreement, trusted executable binding, drift refusal, and fixture identity. |\\n12315:| Compatibility covers old/new readers, mixed peers, unsupported/unknown backends, bootstrap, and restore | Sections 4.B–4.E, 6.5, 7.A, 11.9, 14.6, and 17.2–17.4 define exact legacy translations, inert browse/sync, writer-version negotiation, no silent restore fallback, and no coercion. |\\n12416:| Configuration | Sections 6.2, 6.4, and 6.5 TOML plus Section 3.2 path registry | Add root <code>unknown_root</code>; add secret value or raw backend command/environment; set unsafe SSH host-key bypass; exercise all flags/environment values plus empty and unknown <code>AX_*</code> cases; reject Config-2 directory bounds, Config-3 duplicate/unknown/backend-policy/trust violations, restore fallback, silent major rewrite, or downgrade mutation |\\n12417:| Provider protocol | Section 7.2 envelopes, every Section 7.5 row, and Section 7.A v3 descriptor | Mismatch request ID; success with both body/error; operation/body tag mismatch; stale/mismatched Terminal Instance binding; v2 projection of a non-built-in ID; compatible/major/invalid-first-output Error binding fixtures |\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3747,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 937,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
