{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c66b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":400,"recorded_at":1780531400000795,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"3372bf67-eac6-49d2-9920-be3556dd30a0"},"task_id":"3372bf67-eac6-49d2-9920-be3556dd30a0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"3372bf67-eac6-49d2-9920-be3556dd30a0","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(3451 line(s) above)\n3452|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3453|\n3454|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3455|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3456|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3457|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3458|\n3459|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3460|| --- | --- |\n3461|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3462|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3463|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3464|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3465|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3466|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3467|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3468|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3469|\n3470|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3471|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3472|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3473|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3474|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3475|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3476|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3477|\n3478|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3479|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3480|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3481|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3482|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3483|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3484|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3485|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3486|\n3487|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3488|\n3489|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3490|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3491|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3492|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3493|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3494|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3495|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3496|\n3497|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3498|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3499|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3500|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3501|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3502|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3503|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3504|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3505|\n3506|The closed operation registry is:\n3507|\n3508|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3509|| --- | --- |\n3510|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3511|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3512|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3513|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3514|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3515|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3516|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3517|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3518|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3519|\n3520|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3521|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3522|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3523|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3524|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3525|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3526|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3527|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3528|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3529|every candidate object.\n3530|\n3531|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n3532|<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\n3533|<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\n3534|Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n3535|embedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\n3536|\n3537|- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\n3538|  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3539|  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n3540|  <code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3541|  <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>, <code>request_digest:digest</code>,\n3542|  and <code>extensions</code>. The host constructs it from the verified\n3543|  candidate. <code>request_digest</code> is the digest of the JCS request body\n3544|  with only that member omitted. Every success echoes the context byte-for-byte.\n3545|- <code>ReadAuthority</code> contains exactly <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3546|  <code>purpose:source_native|target_staged|target_live</code>,\n3547|  <code>root_handle_names:sorted unique string[1..128][1..128]</code>,\n3548|  <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Handle names\n3549|  identify host-opened descriptors or handles delivered out of band; they are\n3550|  never paths.\n3551|- <code>ObjectAuthority</code> contains exactly\n3552|  <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3553|  <code>purpose:capture_plan|raw_source|canonical_source|projection_plan|projected_target|read_back_evidence</code>,\n3554|  <code>mode:read|fresh_sink</code>, <code>max_objects:uint53</code>,\n3555|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3556|  <code>fresh_sink</code> requires an empty host-created sink and both limits\n3557|  greater than zero. <code>read</code> exposes only request-named objects.\n3558|- <code>SourceSelector</code> contains exactly\n3559|  <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n3560|  <code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and\n3561|  <code>opaque_source_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>; exactly one is non-null.\n3562|- <code>AdapterFinding</code> contains exactly\n3563|  <code>severity:info|warning|error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n3564|  <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3565|  <code>remediation:string[1..4096]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3566|- <code>ResourceLimits</code> contains exactly\n3567|  <code>max_objects:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3568|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3569|  <code>max_single_object_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3570|  <code>max_events:uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n3571|  <code>max_target_resources:uint53[0..65536]</code>. Each per-item maximum is\n3572|  no greater than <code>max_total_bytes</code>.\n3573|- <code>CapturePlanItem</code> contains exactly\n3574|  <code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n3575|  <code>class:capture-class</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n3576|  <code>required:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3577|\n3578|The exact request and success <code>body</code> registry is:\n3579|\n3580|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3581|| --- | --- | --- |\n(more lines below)"}}}
