{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6ef","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":466,"recorded_at":1780531400000927,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"99fd9134-1cdc-48df-b313-995306850c18"},"task_id":"99fd9134-1cdc-48df-b313-995306850c18","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"99fd9134-1cdc-48df-b313-995306850c18","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-17-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"inventory\\\\|derived\\\\|grammar\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head -n 20; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"tracecheck\\\" --include=\\\"*.json\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" -l . 2>/dev/null | grep -v specdoc | head; echo ===; ls internal/traceability/cmd/\",\n  \"description\": \"Find logbook inventory rule and tracecheck\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"scan_scope_hint\": \"[hint] unscoped recursive scan over the workspace root — scope the next search to the subtree the task names or use the bounded search tool; if this scan backgrounded, harvest or terminate it before ending the turn.\",\n  \"output\": \"45:- EVIDENCE: `go test ./...` exit 0 (14 packages), `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean; terminalbackend 89.3%, config 94.7% statement coverage. Every refusal gate narrowed (grammar widened one rule at a time; drift changes one record member at a time); `TestErrorPredicatesAreExclusive` proves one wire code per refusal; duplicate/drift refusals assert the admitted record is unchanged. Wire codes verified against the pinned catalog vocabulary in-test.\\n52:- SCOPE: new `internal/cliresult/guards_test.go` and `internal/cliresult/guard_inventory_test.go`, one production fix in `internal/cliresult/client.go`, `README.md`, `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json` and its projection digest. Round-7 rework of TASK-260830-33sfxc after review; §1.6, §14.2, §15.1, §15.2, §17.2.\\n71:- FIX: `TestTheCodeToExitStatusAgreementIsMeasuredOverTheWholeCodeRegistry` drives all 316 registered codes across the 4 registered versions at all 17 registered failure statuses — 5,372 rows. The agreeing status must be ADMITTED and each of the other sixteen refused with this guard's own sentence naming both numbers, so a pair settled by `decodeExitStatus`, by the closed member set, or by the retryability gate does not count as coverage of it. Per-version totals are pinned at 752, 1,056, 1,504 and 1,744 and re-derived from `CodesFor` and `CodesByExitStatus`.\\n94:### 1338 — A figure published beside a measurement must be derived from it, not restated next to it: third instance in one artifact\\n101:- DECISION: the pin polices its own completeness. Every digit run in the paragraph that no pinned phrase consumed is reported as unmeasured, with only dotted version and path tokens exempt under a deliberately narrow rule. That makes DELETING a row from the pinned-figure list a red rather than a quietly smaller comparison — the failure mode entry 2113 records for a derived gate that did not police its own extraction pattern.\\n139:- FINDING: the first draft of this fix cited Section 1.6 as fixing the wire format as \\\"UTF-8 JSON restricted to the common logical data model\\\". **That sentence is nowhere in the pinned document** — a paraphrase wearing quotation marks, caught by checking the citation through `internal/specdoc` instead of trusting the wording. The two real fragments, `SPEC.md:218` \\\"map keys MUST be UTF-8 strings and MUST be unique\\\" and `SPEC.md:221` \\\"floating-point numbers, NaN, Infinity, non-string map keys, and duplicate keys are forbidden\\\", are now located BY CONTENT and their section is re-derived, so the citation survives re-pagination; the absence of the paraphrase is asserted too, so the correction cannot be undone by someone who remembers the wording. Same class as the 0559 false-citation entry, one contract over.\\n237:- FINDING: a doc comment cannot be pinned by a test that *restates* it — that just moves the same unverified claim into a second file where it can drift identically. The pin only works if the comment is the test's **input**. `canonical_number_contract_test.go` parses the `literal -> canonical` rows and the exported entry-point names out of the `Canonicalize` doc with `go/parser` and checks them against real behaviour and against the entry-point set derived from the production call graph. Editing prose without code reddens (M3, M4); editing code without prose reddens (M5). An indented line in the comment that is neither a row nor an exported name is a hard failure, so documented-but-unchecked text cannot accumulate.\\n239:- REGRESSION AVOIDED: the first draft derived its own AST call graph recording only `call.Fun.(*ast.Ident)` edges and skipping methods — the identical construction the 0210 entry measured at 3 of 7 UTF-8 guards while it looked complete. Rewritten to reuse `productionCallGraph`/`exportedProductionEntryPoints`/`reachableProductionFunctions` from `utf8_subsumption_test.go`. Shipping a second, weaker graph beside the hardened one would have reopened a blind spot this board had already paid to close, in the same package, three hours later.\\n240:- EVIDENCE: six mutants, each confirmed present in the source before its test was measured. M1 **narrows** rather than deletes — `integer > maxSafeInteger` → `maxSafeInteger+2`, gate still in place, bound moved by two — and the negative test still catches `9007199254740993`. M2 deletes the gate. M3/M4 drift the doc. M5 makes `Canonicalize` call `validateAXNumbers` and the derived set correctly grows to include `CanonicalByteLength`. M6 registers `validateAXNumbers` in a function-value table and routes the gate through it: **behaviour unchanged, `go build` exit 0, negative test still green at exit 0**, and only `TestValidateAXNumbersHasNoCallSiteThisGraphCannotSee` reddens.\\n241:- FINDING: M6 is what separates a stated bound from a held one. The graph resolves a computed callee to every function whose identifier is used as a value in the package, so the derived entry-point set is exact *only while* `validateAXNumbers` is never used as a value. That precondition is not narration — it is the single test standing between a dispatch-table registration and a silently widened set with the whole suite `ok`.\\n248:- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/traceability` proved two things about a `section_binding` — the named Go declaration parses and exists, and the linked acceptance case is registered with an executable test. Neither compares the implementation against the section it claims, so a sliver satisfied a whole-section binding and `tracecheck -section X` reported it as owned. `section:2.2` (22 unconditional lease/replica invariants) was bound to `validateSessionRecordCommon`, which validates one enum and a name grammar; `section:18.4` (audit retention) was bound to `OpenProjection`, and no retention code exists. Three independently produced branches reached that state without anyone noticing.\\n250:- FIX: every `section_binding` declares a `coverage` level and the gate recomputes it. Denominator measured from `internal/specdoc` — RFC 2119 clause lines under the heading *and its subheadings*, so a parent is measured over its children. Numerator = the clauses the binding enumerates, each of which must index that inventory, declare its exact `SPEC.md` line, quote it verbatim beginning on that line, and name an acceptance case the binding itself owns. Declared level must equal the measured bucket. Assigned-scope admission now requires `full`; repository-wide verification stays green on an honest registry.\\n272:### 0210 — A derived call graph that only sees `f(x)` covers 3 of 7 guards and looks complete\\n288:- DECISION: two citations are exempted by name, line, and written reason rather than by widening the rule — both Session Record majors cite the Section 2.1 Terms row `Session name`, because the Session Record clause defers the name grammar to a section reference that contains no grammar. An unused exemption reddens, and removing either one reddens the shipped artifact, so they are load-bearing and disclosed, not decoration.\\n290:- EVIDENCE: 14 sibling retargets derived from the document itself — every shared-member pair of the Section 10.4 Git table, both directions — each planted into a copy of the shipped artifact and each required to be refused by the sibling's name. Six mutants run in a throwaway `git archive` copy, all confirmed present before measurement: deleting the anchor reddens all 15 sibling and field plants; narrowing it to `Type` tables only reddens the field-table plant; restoring one of the seven pre-fix citations reddens and names the row and GitHead; removing the table-row boundary reddens both the specdoc and the artifact stitch tests; removing one declaring pin reddens 8 shipped rows rather than granting a free pass; a stale pin and a stale exemption both redden. Class re-scan over all 347 rows: 357 citations, 235 on table body rows, 0 naming another type, 2 naming another member and both exempted by name.\\n296:- ROOT CAUSE: `sessionRecordGrammarFamily` classified a constraint enumeration row into an executable grammar family by substring-matching the row's `Pinned SPEC declaration` prose. That column is the fidelity artifact 0022 rewrote. Replacing informative-but-partly-fabricated prose with verbatim `SPEC.md` fragments removed the words the classifier greps for, so eight rows fell out of `TestSessionRecordDeclaredGrammarRowsReachIdentityProductionEntries` and stopped being attacked with invalid grammar values through both public identity entries. Measured on both trees with the same command: 18 rows -> 11, 107 subtests -> 66, `reverse-dns` 11 -> 4.\\n297:- FINDING: the completeness check was `familyCounts[family] == 0`. Four is not zero, so a 64% narrowing of the largest family reported nothing. A non-empty guard on a derived set is the same defect class as the non-empty guard on the excerpt column that 0022 exists to remove — one level up, in the gate doing the removing.\\n298:- FINDING: `Session Record Launch Plan.env_names` was a pure regression. Its new excerpt at `:1490` quotes the grammar verbatim, `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}` included; nothing about its fidelity changed. It left only because the classifier greps for the words \\\"environment names\\\", which the true quote does not contain.\\n306:- FIX: anchor the citation to a clause. `specdoc.SectionID` resolves a line to its nearest enclosing numbered heading (an unnumbered subheading opens no clause), and each shape pins the clauses its citations may use. Measured before pinning: all 40 shapes' citations already clustered in exactly one clause, except the two Session Record majors, which legitimately cite 2.1 as well as 5.1 for the Terms-table name grammar. The pinned shape set is asserted exactly against the artifact, so a new shape must declare its clause. `TestClauseAnchorRefusesEveryForeignSectionForOneRow` plants a verbatim line from each of the 11 other clauses into one row: 11 of 11 refused, shipped row still admitted.\\n328:- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/canonicaljson/constraint_inventory_test.go` derived shape, member and call site from the production `requireExactMembers` argument lists and compared them both ways, but required the `Pinned SPEC declaration` column only to be `!= \\\"\\\"`. Artifact and code could be wrong about the contract together and stay green. A self-consistency proof wearing fidelity-proof clothes.\\n===\\n./LOGBOOK.md\\n./task-board.config.json\\n./internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json\\n./internal/canonicaljson/testdata/closed-vocabularies.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260902-24e45b/TASK-260902-24e45b_review-verdict.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260902-24e45b/TASK-260902-24e45b_reapply-report.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-34elja/TASK-260830-34elja_results.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-34elja/TASK-260830-34elja_review-verdict-rev2.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-34elja/TASK-260830-34elja_review-verdict.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-34elja/TASK-260830-34elja_rework-rev2.md\\n===\\ntracecheck\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 10979,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2745,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
