{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c703","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":476,"recorded_at":1780531400000947,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"call_id":"call_01a06f2f040b70709fb87c541dc2f0cb","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-17-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"inventory\\\\|derived\\\\|grammar\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head -n 20; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"tracecheck\\\" --include=\\\"*.json\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" -l . 2>/dev/null | grep -v specdoc | head; echo ===; ls internal/traceability/cmd/\",\n  \"description\": \"Find logbook inventory rule and tracecheck\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"scan_scope_hint\": \"[hint] unscoped recursive scan over the workspace root — scope the next search to the subtree the task names or use the bounded search tool; if this scan backgrounded, harvest or terminate it before ending the turn.\",\n  \"output\": \"45:- EVIDENCE: `go test ./...` exit 0 (14 packages), `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean; terminalbackend 89.3%, config 94.7% statement coverage. Every refusal gate narrowed (grammar widened one rule at a time; drift changes one record member at a time); `TestErrorPredicatesAreExclusive` proves one wire code per refusal; duplicate/drift refusals assert the admitted record is unchanged. Wire codes verified against the pinned catalog vocabulary in-test.\\n52:- SCOPE: new `internal/cliresult/guards_test.go` and `internal/cliresult/guard_inventory_test.go`, one production fix in `internal/cliresult/client.go`, `README.md`, `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json` and its projection digest. Round-7 rework of TASK-260830-33sfxc after review; §1.6, §14.2, §15.1, §15.2, §17.2.\\n71:- FIX: `TestTheCodeToExitStatusAgreementIsMeasuredOverTheWholeCodeRegistry` drives all 316 registered codes across the 4 registered versions at all 17 registered failure statuses — 5,372 rows. The agreeing status must be ADMITTED and each of the other sixteen refused with this guard's own sentence naming both numbers, so a pair settled by `decodeExitStatus`, by the closed member set, or by the retryability gate does not count as coverage of it. Per-version totals are pinned at 752, 1,056, 1,504 and 1,744 and re-derived from `CodesFor` and `CodesByExitStatus`.\\n94:### 1338 — A figure published beside a measurement must be derived from it, not restated next to it: third instance in one artifact\\n101:- DECISION: the pin polices its own completeness. Every digit run in the paragraph that no pinned phrase consumed is reported as unmeasured, with only dotted version and path tokens exempt under a deliberately narrow rule. That makes DELETING a row from the pinned-figure list a red rather than a quietly smaller comparison — the failure mode entry 2113 records for a derived gate that did not police its own extraction pattern.\\n139:- FINDING: the first draft of this fix cited Section 1.6 as fixing the wire format as \\\"UTF-8 JSON restricted to the common logical data model\\\". **That sentence is nowhere in the pinned document** — a paraphrase wearing quotation marks, caught by checking the citation through `internal/specdoc` instead of trusting the wording. The two real fragments, `SPEC.md:218` \\\"map keys MUST be UTF-8 strings and MUST be unique\\\" and `SPEC.md:221` \\\"floating-point numbers, NaN, Infinity, non-string map keys, and duplicate keys are forbidden\\\", are now located BY CONTENT and their section is re-derived, so the citation survives re-pagination; the absence of the paraphrase is asserted too, so the correction cannot be undone by someone who remembers the wording. Same class as the 0559 false-citation entry, one contract over.\\n237:- FINDING: a doc comment cannot be pinned by a test that *restates* it — that just moves the same unverified claim into a second file where it can drift identically. The pin only works if the comment is the test's **input**. `canonical_number_contract_test.go` parses the `literal -> canonical` rows and the exported entry-point names out of the `Canonicalize` doc with `go/parser` and checks them against real behaviour and against the entry-point set derived from the production call graph. Editing prose without code reddens (M3, M4); editing code without prose reddens (M5). An indented line in the comment that is neither a row nor an exported name is a hard failure, so documented-but-unchecked text cannot accumulate.\\n239:- REGRESSION AVOIDED: the first draft derived its own AST call graph recording only `call.Fun.(*ast.Ident)` edges and skipping methods — the identical construction the 0210 entry measured at 3 of 7 UTF-8 guards while it looked complete. Rewritten to reuse `productionCallGraph`/`exportedProductionEntryPoints`/`reachableProductionFunctions` from `utf8_subsumption_test.go`. Shipping a second, weaker graph beside the hardened one would have reopened a blind spot this board had already paid to close, in the same package, three hours later.\\n240:- EVIDENCE: six mutants, each confirmed present in the source before its test was measured. M1 **narrows** rather than deletes — `integer > maxSafeInteger` → `maxSafeInteger+2`, gate still in place, bound moved by two — and the negative test still catches `9007199254740993`. M2 deletes the gate. M3/M4 drift the doc. M5 makes `Canonicalize` call `validateAXNumbers` and the derived set correctly grows to include `CanonicalByteLength`. M6 registers `validateAXNumbers` in a function-value table and routes the gate through it: **behaviour unchanged, `go build` exit 0, negative test still green at exit 0**, and only `TestValidateAXNumbersHasNoCallSiteThisGraphCannotSee` reddens.\\n241:- FINDING: M6 is what separates a stated bound from a held one. The graph resolves a computed callee to every function whose identifier is used as a value in the package, so the derived entry-point set is exact *only while* `validateAXNumbers` is never used as a value. That precondition is not narration — it is the single test standing between a dispatch-table registration and a silently widened set with the whole suite `ok`.\\n248:- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/traceability` proved two things about a `section_binding` — the named Go declaration parses and exists, and the linked acceptance case is registered with an executable test. Neither compares the implementation against the section it claims, so a sliver satisfied a whole-section binding and `tracecheck -section X` reported it as owned. `section:2.2` (22 unconditional lease/replica invariants) was bound to `validateSessionRecordCommon`, which validates one enum and a name grammar; `section:18.4` (audit retention) was bound to `OpenProjection`, and no retention code exists. Three independently produced branches reached that state without anyone noticing.\\n250:- FIX: every `section_binding` declares a `coverage` level and the gate recomputes it. Denominator measured from `internal/specdoc` — RFC 2119 clause lines under the heading *and its subheadings*, so a parent is measured over its children. Numerator = the clauses the binding enumerates, each of which must index that inventory, declare its exact `SPEC.md` line, quote it verbatim beginning on that line, and name an acceptance case the binding itself owns. Declared level must equal the measured bucket. Assigned-scope admission now requires `full`; repository-wide verification stays green on an honest registry.\\n272:### 0210 — A derived call graph that only sees `f(x)` covers 3 of 7 guards and looks complete\\n288:- DECISION: two citations are exempted by name, line, and written reason rather than by widening the rule — both Session Record majors cite the Section 2.1 Terms row `Session name`, because the Session Record clause defers the name grammar to a section reference that contains no grammar. An unused exemption reddens, and removing either one reddens the shipped artifact, so they are load-bearing and disclosed, not decoration.\\n290:- EVIDENCE: 14 sibling retargets derived from the document itself — every shared-member pair of the Section 10.4 Git table, both directions — each planted into a copy of the shipped artifact and each required to be refused by the sibling's name. Six mutants run in a throwaway `git archive` copy, all confirmed present before measurement: deleting the anchor reddens all 15 sibling and field plants; narrowing it to `Type` tables only reddens the field-table plant; restoring one of the seven pre-fix citations reddens and names the row and GitHead; removing the table-row boundary reddens both the specdoc and the artifact stitch tests; removing one declaring pin reddens 8 shipped rows rather than granting a free pass; a stale pin and a stale exemption both redden. Class re-scan over all 347 rows: 357 citations, 235 on table body rows, 0 naming another type, 2 naming another member and both exempted by name.\\n296:- ROOT CAUSE: `sessionRecordGrammarFamily` classified a constraint enumeration row into an executable grammar family by substring-matching the row's `Pinned SPEC declaration` prose. That column is the fidelity artifact 0022 rewrote. Replacing informative-but-partly-fabricated prose with verbatim `SPEC.md` fragments removed the words the classifier greps for, so eight rows fell out of `TestSessionRecordDeclaredGrammarRowsReachIdentityProductionEntries` and stopped being attacked with invalid grammar values through both public identity entries. Measured on both trees with the same command: 18 rows -> 11, 107 subtests -> 66, `reverse-dns` 11 -> 4.\\n297:- FINDING: the completeness check was `familyCounts[family] == 0`. Four is not zero, so a 64% narrowing of the largest family reported nothing. A non-empty guard on a derived set is the same defect class as the non-empty guard on the excerpt column that 0022 exists to remove — one level up, in the gate doing the removing.\\n298:- FINDING: `Session Record Launch Plan.env_names` was a pure regression. Its new excerpt at `:1490` quotes the grammar verbatim, `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}` included; nothing about its fidelity changed. It left only because the classifier greps for the words \\\"environment names\\\", which the true quote does not contain.\\n306:- FIX: anchor the citation to a clause. `specdoc.SectionID` resolves a line to its nearest enclosing numbered heading (an unnumbered subheading opens no clause), and each shape pins the clauses its citations may use. Measured before pinning: all 40 shapes' citations already clustered in exactly one clause, except the two Session Record majors, which legitimately cite 2.1 as well as 5.1 for the Terms-table name grammar. The pinned shape set is asserted exactly against the artifact, so a new shape must declare its clause. `TestClauseAnchorRefusesEveryForeignSectionForOneRow` plants a verbatim line from each of the 11 other clauses into one row: 11 of 11 refused, shipped row still admitted.\\n328:- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/canonicaljson/constraint_inventory_test.go` derived shape, member and call site from the production `requireExactMembers` argument lists and compared them both ways, but required the `Pinned SPEC declaration` column only to be `!= \\\"\\\"`. Artifact and code could be wrong about the contract together and stay green. A self-consistency proof wearing fidelity-proof clothes.\\n===\\n./LOGBOOK.md\\n./task-board.config.json\\n./internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json\\n./internal/canonicaljson/testdata/closed-vocabularies.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260902-24e45b/TASK-260902-24e45b_review-verdict.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260902-24e45b/TASK-260902-24e45b_reapply-report.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-34elja/TASK-260830-34elja_results.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-34elja/TASK-260830-34elja_review-verdict-rev2.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-34elja/TASK-260830-34elja_review-verdict.md\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-34elja/TASK-260830-34elja_rework-rev2.md\\n===\\ntracecheck\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 10979,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2745,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c705","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":477,"recorded_at":1780531400000949,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"call_id":"call_01a06f2f06987a41889ef4ebeb02fff9","text":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/manifest_pin_test.go`.\n1|// White-box pins for reconciliation arms no document can deliver an input\n2|// to. Parse enforces registry-row equality for every claim (a Manifest or\n3|// Probe cannot redefine a row), so a drifted override or addition fails at\n4|// the document gate before Reconcile runs; likewise, same-ID\n5|// differing-bytes evidence cannot pass parsing because the ID is a hash of\n6|// the bytes. These arms are measured here, at the guard, with typed values\n7|// mutated after parsing, rather than left as prose; the reachability bound\n8|// is stated, not inferred.\n9|package terminalbackend\n10|\n11|import (\n12|\t\"encoding/json\"\n13|\t\"errors\"\n14|\t\"sort\"\n15|\t\"testing\"\n16|\t\"time\"\n17|)\n18|\n19|// pinVerifier accepts every attestation: signature validity is owned by the\n20|// black-box suite with real cryptography, and these pins must not depend\n21|// on it.\n22|func pinVerifier(issuerID string, message, signature []byte) error { return nil }\n23|\n24|// requirePinRefusal asserts the exact refusal clause, for the same reason\n25|// the black-box suite names its arms: most gates share one wire code, so a\n26|// code-only pin cannot hold the gate it names.\n27|func requirePinRefusal(t *testing.T, err error, wantCode, wantDetail string) {\n28|\tt.Helper()\n29|\n30|\tvar refusal *Error\n31|\tif !errors.As(err, &refusal) {\n32|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"error = %v, want *Error with code %q at %q\", err, wantCode, wantDetail)\n33|\t}\n34|\tif refusal.Code != wantCode || refusal.Detail != wantDetail {\n35|\t\tt.Errorf(\"refusal = %q at %q, want %q at %q\", refusal.Code, refusal.Detail, wantCode, wantDetail)\n36|\t}\n37|}\n38|\n39|// TestReconcileRefusesDriftedOverride pins the override registry-binding\n40|// arm: a probed override of a variable claim whose row members drift from\n41|// the manifest row is refused, even though Parse would already refuse the\n42|// document carrying it.\n43|func TestReconcileRefusesDriftedOverride(t *testing.T) {\n44|\tt.Parallel()\n45|\n46|\tmanifest, probe, evidence := validReconcileTriple(t)\n47|\tfor index := range probe.CapabilityClaims {\n48|\t\tif probe.CapabilityClaims[index].Capability == \"headless_creation\" {\n49|\t\t\tprobe.CapabilityClaims[index].DependentOperations = []string{\"create\", \"status\"}\n50|\t\t}\n51|\t}\n52|\t_, err := Reconcile(manifest, probe, evidence, \"generation-alpha\", testAdmissionTime(), pinVerifier)\n53|\trequirePinRefusal(t, err, CodeMismatch, \"probe override registry binding\")\n54|}\n55|\n56|// TestReconcileRefusesDriftedAddition pins the addition registry-binding\n57|// arm: a probed addition whose row members drift from the closed registry\n58|// row is refused, even though Parse would already refuse the document.\n59|func TestReconcileRefusesDriftedAddition(t *testing.T) {\n60|\tt.Parallel()\n61|\n62|\tmanifest, probe, evidence := validReconcileTriple(t)\n63|\tfor index := range probe.CapabilityClaims {\n64|\t\tif probe.CapabilityClaims[index].Capability == \"graceful_stop\" {\n65|\t\t\tprobe.CapabilityClaims[index].EvidenceRequirements = []string{\"conformance_fixture\"}\n66|\t\t}\n67|\t}\n68|\t_, err := Reconcile(manifest, probe, evidence, \"generation-alpha\", testAdmissionTime(), pinVerifier)\n69|\trequirePinRefusal(t, err, CodeMismatch, \"probe addition registry binding\")\n70|}\n71|\n72|// TestReconcileRefusesConflictingEvidence pins the same-ID conflict arm:\n73|// two evidence objects sharing an ID but carrying different facts\n74|// invalidate the whole probe. This input cannot arrive through Parse\n75|// (identical IDs over different bytes fail the identity recomputation),\n76|// so it is constructed at the typed level.\n77|func TestReconcileRefusesConflictingEvidence(t *testing.T) {\n78|\tt.Parallel()\n79|\n80|\tmanifest, probe, evidence := validReconcileTriple(t)\n81|\ttwin := evidence[0]\n82|\ttwin.Facts = []string{\"fixture_passed\", \"runtime_probe_passed\", \"ui_absent\"}\n83|\tevidence = append(evidence, twin)\n84|\t_, err := Reconcile(manifest, probe, evidence, \"generation-alpha\", testAdmissionTime(), pinVerifier)\n85|\trequirePinRefusal(t, err, CodeMismatch, \"conflicting evidence\")\n86|}\n87|\n88|// TestIdenticalDuplicateEvidenceDeduped pins the stated dedup bound: an\n89|// evidence object supplied twice byte-for-byte contributes its ID once and\n90|// admits. (Attestation signatures are deterministic for one key and\n91|// message, so identical documents are genuinely identical inputs, not two\n92|// observations.) Same-ID differing-bytes input stays refused above.\n93|func TestIdenticalDuplicateEvidenceDeduped(t *testing.T) {\n94|\tt.Parallel()\n95|\n96|\tmanifest, probe, evidence := validReconcileTriple(t)\n97|\tevidence = append(evidence, evidence[0], evidence[1])\n98|\tadmitted, err := Reconcile(manifest, probe, evidence, \"generation-alpha\", testAdmissionTime(), pinVerifier)\n99|\tif err != nil {\n100|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Reconcile() error = %v\", err)\n101|\t}\n102|\tif len(admitted.EvidenceIDs) != 2 {\n103|\t\tt.Errorf(\"EvidenceIDs = %v, want 2 deduplicated IDs\", admitted.EvidenceIDs)\n104|\t}\n105|}\n106|\n107|// TestReconcileRefusesExecutableSubstitution pins the digest-identity arm:\n108|// a probe whose executable digest differs from the manifest member is\n109|// untrusted, even though both documents parse (each is valid against its\n110|// own kind rule). Parse cannot see across documents, so this arm is\n111|// reachable only here and in production admission.\n112|func TestReconcileRefusesExecutableSubstitution(t *testing.T) {\n113|\tt.Parallel()\n114|\n115|\tmanifest, probe, evidence := validExternalPinTriple(t)\n116|\tprobe.ExecutableDigest = testPinDigest(0xE6)\n117|\t_, err := Reconcile(manifest, probe, evidence, \"generation-alpha\", testAdmissionTime(), pinVerifier)\n118|\trequirePinRefusal(t, err, CodeUntrusted, \"executable substitution\")\n119|}\n120|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
