{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c725","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":493,"recorded_at":1780531400000981,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"1443425f-f9f4-4865-8919-f9b80b34fc4d"},"task_id":"1443425f-f9f4-4865-8919-f9b80b34fc4d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"1443425f-f9f4-4865-8919-f9b80b34fc4d","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-18-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"guard_inventory\\\\|refusal.*inventory\\\\|inventory.*refusal\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head; echo ===; ls internal/cliresult/ 2>/dev/null; echo ===; grep -c \\\"\\\" internal/canonicaljson/grammar_inventory_test.go internal/cliresult/guard_inventory_test.go 2>/dev/null\",\n  \"description\": \"Find inventory test models\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"52:- SCOPE: new `internal/cliresult/guards_test.go` and `internal/cliresult/guard_inventory_test.go`, one production fix in `internal/cliresult/client.go`, `README.md`, `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json` and its projection digest. Round-7 rework of TASK-260830-33sfxc after review; §1.6, §14.2, §15.1, §15.2, §17.2.\\n352:- SCOPE: `internal/canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go` (production), `grammar_inventory_test.go`, `member_shape_refusal_test.go`, `session_record_versions_test.go`, `testdata/constraint-enumeration.md`, `README.md`.\\n399:- DECISION: extracted `verifyBlobContent` in `internal/localstore/blob_inspection.go` as the single owner of \\\"read this digest-path entry and report what that proved\\\", returning a `blobVerdict` whose zero value `blobUnproven` is deliberately not a proof. Both `inspectExisting` and `scanAuthoritativeBlobs` now consult it; each still maps the verdict onto its own consequence, so the projection's two `projectionRefusal` call sites stay in `projection.go` where the derived refusal inventory can still demand a negative path for them.\\n421:- ROOT CAUSE of why every existing gate stayed green: mutation testing cannot surface an ABSENT clause. There is no operator to rewrite, no literal to shift, no guard to delete. The 47-call-site vocabulary sweep, the derived refusal-coverage gate, the declared-bounds inventory and five seeded fuzz corpora were all satisfied by a validator missing a third of one normative sentence. It was found by reading the spec sentence against the code, which is the only method that finds a clause that is not there.\\n549:- FINDING: a derived mutation sweep that admitted **one extra member** at each of the 47 closed-vocabulary call sites in `internal/canonicaljson` survived **47 out of 47 times**. `go test ./...`, all four seeded fuzz corpora, `tracecheck`, the derived declared-bounds inventory and the derived refusal-guard coverage gate were all green while, for example, `validateLeaseRecord` admitted a fifth lease reason and `validateObservationEvent` admitted a sixth result.\\n578:- CORRECTION: two artifacts overclaimed and are fixed rather than left standing. `TestEverySessionEventClosedVocabularyRefusesComplementAtProductionEntries` said \\\"Every\\\" over a hand-maintained list missing `accepted_risks`; its subject is now derived from the pinned payload inventory (21 hand-listed → 24 derived). The revision-3 LOGBOOK claim that a derived sweep over \\\"all refusal guards\\\" found 8 survivors does not reproduce and has been corrected in place.\\n690:- FINDING: A derived refusal inventory can prove a site was reached. It cannot prove the site decided the outcome. Those are different facts, and positive-path-only coverage of a refusal looks identical to real coverage in both the inventory and the mutant count until the fixture is built so that every preceding check passes.\\n699:- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/localstore/projection_refusal_inventory_test.go` derived expected refusal sites from the production AST but matched only `*ast.Ident` calls named `projectionRefusal`. Six live clauses written as bare `fmt.Errorf(\\\"%w: ...\\\", ErrUnsafeOwnership)` or as delegated `verifyOwnerFileInfo`/`verifyOwnerDirectory` guards were invisible to the gate whose job was to notice them, and shipped unpinned while 20+ funnelled sites were enforced.\\n704:- SCOPE: `internal/localstore/projection.go`, `projection_lock_unix.go`, `projection_refusal_inventory_test.go`, new `projection_unix_test.go`, `README.md`.\\n===\\nbodies_test.go\\nbodies.go\\nclient_test.go\\nclient.go\\ncliresult_test.go\\ncliresult.go\\ncommand.go\\nconfirmation_test.go\\ndatamodel_test.go\\ndecode_test.go\\ndecode.go\\nelements_test.go\\nenvelope_test.go\\nfixtures_test.go\\nflags_test.go\\nflags.go\\nguard_inventory_test.go\\nguards_test.go\\nhistorical_test.go\\nidentifiers_test.go\\noutput_test.go\\noutput.go\\nprecedence_test.go\\nrefusal_test.go\\nrelabel_test.go\\nstreams_test.go\\nsubsumption_test.go\\ntestdata\\ntypeconfusion_test.go\\ntypes.go\\nvalue.go\\n===\\ninternal/canonicaljson/grammar_inventory_test.go:1308\\ninternal/cliresult/guard_inventory_test.go:542\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4066,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1017,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
