ion:7.A\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.A; no clause of 7.A is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 2 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n}\\n---\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:13.14.5\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"validateSessionEventV2\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\",\\n  \\\"core-record-identity-validation\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unmeasured\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"validateSessionEventV2 validates the Section 13.14.5 v2 Session Event shape, which is topically the subject of the section; the RFC 2119 scanner measures no clause line under 13.14.5, because the section states its obligations as required-member and variant tables rather than in uppercase keywords, so the gate cannot measure how much of the section this binding actually discharges.\\\"\\n}\\n---\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:14.2\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/cliresult/output.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Emit\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"cli-result-envelope-exact\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-envelope-refusal\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-body-closure\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-common-flags\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-yes-admission\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-json-one-document\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-destructive-confirmation\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-expectation-flags\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-rpc-serve-rejects-json\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-takeover-adoption\\\",\\n