{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e031","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f2d-c4fb-70c0-8c5e-603ce37ec5f8"},"sequence":3699,"recorded_at":1780531400007393,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02902741-1c1c-40bd-a4a2-4bcb4871f93c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"3ed39323-ba21-4157-9e17-7191c1f9ffb7"},"task_id":"3ed39323-ba21-4157-9e17-7191c1f9ffb7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"3ed39323-ba21-4157-9e17-7191c1f9ffb7","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-132-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat >> LOGBOOK.md <<'EOF'\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef: terminal conformance harness and derived refusal-arm inventory\\n- FINDING: Deriving the refusal arms before writing the inventory found two genuinely unwitnessed arms, not review hypotheticals: `Registry.AdmitProbe` on a nil registry (nil check first, so no fixture needed) and `ParseEvidence` on malformed `observed_at`/`expires_at` (timestamp parse precedes identity recomputation, proven by the new cases passing). Both now have tests. Four more arms are dead by construction with the bound stated, not inferred: two `evidence canonical bytes` arms (serializes a fixed string/bool/null map; `encoding/json` and JCS cannot fail on it) and re-parse `document timestamp` arms after an already-validated member (this leaf's three plus `checkEvidenceLiveness`'s two).\\n- FINDING: The single dynamic-detail funnel is `Registration.validate` wrapping `validatePlatforms` via `err.Error()`. The inventory pins the funneled set exactly (three details, derived from the AST both ways) and allowlists plain-error construction to `validatePlatforms` and `DigestFile` only, with `DigestFile` failures asserted never-`*Error` behaviorally. A second funnel or a new plain-error refusal site is a red.\\n- DECISION: Row resolution is detail-mention OR (entry-mention AND wire-or-verified-predicate-mention), with predicates verified from the production AST. External tests assert codes through predicates with isolating fixtures; demanding detail strings there would misdescribe the battery. Misattribution (right detail, wrong test) remains a review finding — three such rows were caught by reading the generated table, not by the gate.\\n- EVIDENCE: 8 copy-aside mutants, each grep-confirmed present and restored `cmp`-clean: M1 replays the reviewer's exact attack (new arm, new detail) and fails forward naming the arm plus reverse on the count; M2 reuses an existing detail in a new function and fails on the function key; M3/M4/M7 narrow rather than delete and fail at `error = <nil>`; M5 (deleted relay refusal) fails the gate and both inventory directions via the stale row; M6 (swapped legacy map) fails three translation tests; M9 (deleted table row) fails forward plus the bijection. 8/8 killed, 0 survivors.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/conformance.go`, `conformance_test.go`, `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (new); `manifest_test.go` (+2 evidence-timestamp cases), `terminalbackend_test.go` (+5 wire codes); `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json` (+`terminal-lifecycle-conformance` acceptance case, 75->76), `traceability.go` (projection digest), `traceability_test.go`, `cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`, `README.md`. Section bindings untouched: still `unevidenced` with honest gaps, no clause-level claims added.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14 packages), `-race` exit 0 (14 packages), `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0. Package coverage 90.0% statements. New files left untracked in the working tree; no commit (board checkpoints). TASK-260830-1snnef handed to review.\\nEOF\\necho logged\",\n  \"description\": \"Append logbook entry\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"logged\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
